    "narrative": "For this May 21st slate, our offensive engine is anchored by **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.61) and **Tyler Freeman** (66.93). **Geraldo Perdomo** stands as our highest-rated option; despite the dynamic platoon disadvantage against Zach Agnos, he benefits immensely from an assumed #3 spot in the order and a favorable 5.15 xERA matchup, providing a massive 19% bump in our SP skill modeling. **Tyler Freeman** similarly offers a high floor against Eduardo Rodriguez, as his projection gains significant leverage from a 13% SP skill efficiency spike. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.66) remains a staple, his ceiling is slightly capped today by a matchup against Mize and a higher-than-average opposing hold rate that limits his stolen base opportunities, making his reliance on elite batting position and park factors critical to his high output.\n\nIn the outfield, **Lawrence Butler** (58.68) remains our most intriguing play, surging past the marginal threshold due to a strong 13% platoon boost against the right-handed Jos\u00e9 Soriano. He holds the line over **Daulton Varsho** (55.41), who, despite a solid park factor and respectable SP matchup, faces a 10% penalty for his platoon profile against Rod\u00f3n. The decision to bench potential contributors was relatively straightforward today; with **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Bryson Stott**, and **Will Smith** all sidelined by injury or schedule, our bench depth is currently non-existent, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster.\n\nWe are operating with a heightened risk profile due to \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Tyler Freeman**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Geraldo Perdomo**. Should these players shift downward in their respective batting orders, their scores will regress rapidly. We are also monitoring **Masyn Winn** (43.36), who sits at the bottom of our startable tier; while his base projections are decent, the combination of a tough 3.52 xERA matchup and an opposing catcher with an elite 1.89s pop time makes him the most volatile asset in our lineup today. Tread carefully with the stolen base opportunities, as efficiency will be harder to come by if these favorable pitching matchups tighten up mid-game.",
